// A section of sea cliff about 50 m across and 60 m high in grey jointed stone: broad
// flat faces where it has broken along its joints, turned two ways across the cliff, dark
// clefts and chimneys between them, the bedding stepping out as ledges for plants to take
// hold on. Set several side by side, overlapping, into a step in the ground: the ends tuck
// back so the next one hides the join.
// Any number in shape, surface, moss or face may be a (lo, hi) range: each seed lands in it.
